 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "최상급 the -est / the most",
   "en": "Superlatives: the -est / the most"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "셋 이상 중에서 가장 ~한 것은 the + 최상급으로 말합니다. 짧은 형용사는 the + -est(cheap → the cheapest), 긴 형용사는 the most + 형용사(expensive → the most expensive)입니다. good → the best, bad → the worst는 불규칙입니다. 범위는 in the city, in the world, of all로 나타냅니다.",
   "en": "Use the + superlative for the top of three or more. Short adjectives take the + -est (cheap → the cheapest); long adjectives take the most (expensive → the most expensive). Good → the best and bad → the worst are irregular. Show the group with in the city, in the world or of all."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "원형 / Adjective",
    "비교급 / Comparative",
    "최상급 / Superlative"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "cheap",
     "cheaper",
     "the cheapest"
    ],
    [
     "big",
     "bigger",
     "the biggest"
    ],
    [
     "easy",
